## Installation

Requires Unity 2021.3 or later. Installing from a git URL also requires [Git](https://git-scm.com/downloads) on your `PATH`.

### Unity Package Manager (UPM)

1. In Unity, open **Window > Package Manager**.
2. Click the **+** button and select **Add package from git URL** (**Install package from git URL** in Unity 6).
3. Enter the following URL and click **Add** (**Install** in Unity 6):

```text
https://github.com/{{ sdk.gitUserName|url_encode }}/{{ sdk.gitRepoName|url_encode }}.git#{{ sdk.version }}
```

The `#{{ sdk.version }}` suffix pins the package to a release. Change it to any released tag, or omit it to track the latest commit on the default branch.

You can also add the package to `Packages/manifest.json` directly:

```json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "{{ language.params.packageName }}": "https://github.com/{{ sdk.gitUserName|url_encode }}/{{ sdk.gitRepoName|url_encode }}.git#{{ sdk.version }}"
  }
}
```

### Install from disk

1. Download the source code archive of a release from [GitHub](https://github.com/{{ sdk.gitUserName|url_encode }}/{{ sdk.gitRepoName|url_encode }}/releases) and extract it.
2. In **Window > Package Manager**, click the **+** button and select **Add package from disk** (**Install package from disk** in Unity 6).
3. Select the `package.json` file in the extracted folder.
